OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Fri 7 Aug to Sun 16 Aug
OL,6,FProbably rather changeable to begin
OL,7,Fthis period, with some rain or showers
OL,8,Fat times, but also the likelihood of
OL,9,Fsome decent drier interludes too.
OL,10,FTowards mid August, high pressure may
OL,11,Fbecome rather more dominant towards
OL,12,Fthe north of the UK, with lower
OL,13,Fpressure further to the south. This
OL,14,Fmeans there is a greater chance for
OL,15,FAtlantic frontal systems or thundery
OL,16,Finterludes to affect southern areas,
OL,17,Fcertainly in comparison to recent
OL,18,Fweeks, though rainfall amounts could
OL,19,Fbe quite variable with some areas
OL,20,Fseeing relatively little. For the most
OL,21,Fpart, temperatures look to remain
OL,22,Fabove average, especially in the
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,23,Fsouth, though perhaps without the
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
OL,24,Fexceptional heat we have seen in
OL,25,Frecent weeks.
FL,164,160,301,260,100,100
PN,16303
SC,0003
CT,20,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F163A1785683880
OL,1,Wj5hw1~{4k7juhw1{$             G3/3
OL,2,W+.-'"-$/*%*%*%/"-$/*%Q,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Mon 17 Aug to Mon 31 AugFA
OL,6,Fcontinuation of the broad theme of
OL,7,Fhigh pressure remaining in place at
OL,8,Fleast close to the UK, but with
OL,9,Foccasional more unsettled or
OL,10,Fchangeable interludes, either
OL,11,Fresulting from Atlantic frontal
OL,12,Fsystems or thundery plumes. This means
OL,13,Fthat rainfall amounts overall are more
OL,14,Flikely to be below normal than above.
OL,15,FTemperatures will probably be above
OL,16,Faverage and some spells of hot weather
OL,17,Fand heatwaves are possible, especially
OL,18,Fin the south.
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
